  "ai_summary": "IT consultancy stocks are collapsing (-12% monthly, -24% yearly), signaling investors expect AI to automate outsourced IT. Meanwhile, Big Tech headcounts show stable or minor shifts (Meta down 14% yearly, flat monthly), avoiding massive AI-driven labor cuts. Indeed job postings surged 21% yearly but cooled to +0.8% monthly, a leading intent indicator. Anthropic added 44 roles in 30 days, defying AI hoarding fears. Devs aren't cooked. Worrying that AI will take your dev job because consultancy stocks dropped is like panicking about the culinary arts because a frozen pizza factory went bankrupt.",
